{"availability":"available","full":"uCAN-LIN/LinUSBConverter","name":"LinUSBConverter","description":"Open source USB ↔ LIN bus dongle. LIN 2.1 master / slave / monitor, optically isolated, SLCAN compatible — no proprietary drivers.","category":"Other","language":"C","stars":92,"forks":41,"created":"2018-02-10T16:52:33Z","updated":"2026-10-12T17:08:57Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://ucandevices.github.io/ulc.html","topics":["automotive","j2602","lin","lin-bus","open-hardware"],"demo":"https://ucandevices.github.io/ulc.html","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T05:17:07.293Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T05:17:07.293Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T05:17:07.293Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T05:49:27.808Z","stars":92,"forks":41},{"at":"2026-10-12T07:58:33.148Z","stars":92,"forks":41},{"at":"2026-10-17T05:17:07.293Z","stars":92,"forks":41}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The USB LIN Converter (uLC) is a small open-source USB dongle (STM32F042C6, 31 × 18 mm) that lets a PC act as a LIN bus master, slave or passive monitor. It enumerates as a USB CDC virtual COM port and speaks an SLCAN-style ASCII protocol, so it bridges into Linux SocketCAN via slcand and works with parts of can-utils.","A commercial automotive LIN analyzer typically costs hundreds to thousands of euros. This one is around $27 on Tindie.","The LIN protocol implementation is based on openLIN."],"features":["Monitor mode - full frame reception plus single-frame transmission","Master mode - up to 15 scheduled frame slots","Slave mode - up to 15 scheduled frame slots for slave simulation","9600 / 19200 baud rate selection","Optical isolation between LIN and the USB / PC side"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/uCAN-LIN/LinUSBConverter/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"0d6a7617f0cdb50ef2408e5da064a797ed6fa524579e2c450c3dea6b2beba02c","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T05:17:07.378Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T05:17